summary:
- topic: FY2026 Budget Challenges
  text: The Superintendent presented a challenging FY26 budget outlook, noting an
    11.4% local budget increase just to maintain current services. Key constraints
    include reduced reliance on the fund balance, exhausted federal special education
    carryover funds, and decreased federal title funding, necessitating a non-essential
    spending freeze and potential employee position reductions.
- topic: PreK Expansion Initiative
  text: Dr. Prince provided an update on PreK expansion, introducing a new mixed delivery
    model that partners with private childcare facilities. This initiative aims to
    add up to 32 free PreK seats, moving towards universal PreK access for 43% of
    eligible students, at no additional cost to the district through state funding.
- topic: 2025-2026 School Calendar Approval
  text: The board approved the 2025-2026 school calendar, which includes 175 student
    days and 4 staff days. Adjustments were made to accommodate a longer winter break
    and manage potential snow days, with an early release day scheduled before April
    break.
- topic: Athletic Complex Referendum Discussion and Vote
  text: A significant portion of the meeting was dedicated to discussing a proposed
    November 2025 referendum for athletic complex improvements. The Board ultimately
    passed a substitute motion to offer voters a choice between a synthetic turf or
    natural grass stadium field, both including a new track, permanent restrooms,
    and lighting, at a reduced cost compared to the original proposal.
- topic: Community and Staff Perspectives on Athletic Complex
  text: Public comments highlighted concerns about the environmental impact and long-term
    costs of artificial turf, as well as the tax burden on residents, particularly
    seniors. The South Portland Teachers Association (SPTA) advocated for preserving
    student-facing positions in the upcoming budget and ensuring fair contracts for
    educators.
- topic: Board Governance and Policy Review
  text: The board reviewed policies BBA (Roles, Functions, and Duties of School Boards)
    and BCA (School Board Member Ethics) as a follow-up to a previous workshop. The
    Policy Committee also presented updates to copyright compliance and field trip
    policies, including distinctions for local walking trips and gender-neutral language
    revisions.
- topic: Facilities and Operations Updates
  text: The Buildings & Grounds Committee reported on ongoing HVAC issues at the middle
    school, noting that a missing part had been installed and the geothermal system
    was performing well, leading to significant natural gas savings. Appreciation
    was also extended to the custodial staff for maintaining clean schools during
    a challenging time of year.
